  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 410</b></color></size>

    <b>Bronze cannon of Mysore (replica)</b>

    <size=74%>Late 18th century

    <i>Replica of a cast-bronze cannon on a wooden field carriage</i>

    Replica made for this museum</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    Haidar Ali and his son Tipu Sultan built a modern army with European-style artillery cast in their own foundries. Mysore''s forces also used iron-cased war rockets that impressed their British opponents. Many of Tipu''s bronze cannons, decorated with tiger-stripe patterns, were captured in 1799 and are displayed today in Britain and India.</size>

    <size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Replica made for this museum</color></size>'
